{
 "notes": [
  "CHIPs the port adds after the original's 96 (indices 0-95), and its retunes of original CHIPs. docs/CUSTOM_CHIPS.md explains how to recreate or add one: the face picture, the stats and the chatter.",
  "Each family becomes one record per entry of \"chatter\" (the personality table in tables/chatter.json), numbered on from first_index in this order: Cat V 96-100, Cat VI 101-105, Cat VII 106-110, Fox I 111-115, Bear I 116-120, Tortoise I 121-125, Boar I 126-130, Hawk I 131-135, Monkey I 136-140, Meerkat I 141-145, then the bosses' CHIPs of one personality each, Retriever 146 to Labrador 160. Saves and shop days name CHIPs by number, so only ever append families or personalities at the end.",
  "\"stats\" are the original record fields (inner/outer sight shape and size curves, track, lock_frames, weight, critical_percent, dodge_percent = Repulsion Shield chance, knockdown_resistance, price), as in the converted tables/parts.json. A curve is base at level 0, base+mid at its knee and base+top at level 99. Sight sizes stop growing at 999; track is Aim Speed on the port's 0..10 scale (ui/battle_hud.json control).",
  "\"retune\" replaces the listed stats of every original record whose name is in \"names\"; \"why\" records the reason. Delete an entry to get the original's values back.",
  "\"shop\" adds BUY CHIP offers to the given rotating shop day (0-23, garage.json chip_lineups), naming the family and its personality: each day one added cat and one specialist. \"boss_shop\" sells a boss's CHIP (a family whose \"face\" is the boss's portrait cell in the original's atlas) at \"level\" on the calendar days any of its \"contests\" is held, once the player has won one of them; it is offered once a day however many are held. The shop help texts are ui/chip_shop.json and ui/uplift.json chip_help at the same index.",
  "Not applied to S.L.A.I.'s tables, which are another game's."
 ],
